issue(id="0019" status="open")
  title Add an explicit npm build-from-source distribution path
  user-story
    as-a security-conscious JavaScript or web-tooling user
    i-want to install or rebuild puggers from source through npm intentionally
    so-that I can avoid relying only on prebuilt native binaries when my trust model requires local compilation
  premise.
    The default `puggers` npm package should remain convenient and native-backed,
    but serious users may want a deliberate build-from-source path that does not
    depend on trusting published binary artifacts. This path should not hide
    arbitrary install-time compilation in the default package. It should make the
    source artifact, required toolchain, build script permissions, and resulting
    runtime files clear enough for package managers like pnpm and npm to gate or
    approve the native build explicitly.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Decide whether the source-build surface is a separate package, a documented install mode, or both, and record the rationale in the npm packaging docs.
    criterion Define the distributable source artifact shape, including which Rust crates, Cargo metadata, TypeScript files, and lockfiles must be included.
    criterion Add a repeatable npm-accessible build command that compiles the Node-API addon and Rust CLI from source with locked dependencies.
    criterion Ensure the source-build path produces the same runtime layout expected by the existing JavaScript loader and CLI wrapper.
    criterion Document how pnpm and npm users approve or opt into the build scripts required for the source-build path.
    criterion Add tests or CI coverage that installs the source-build artifact in a clean temporary project and verifies both `convertHtmlToPug` and the `puggers` bin.
    criterion Keep the default `puggers` install path free of implicit source compilation unless the policy is explicitly revisited.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Decide between a separate package such as `puggers-source` and an explicit build-from-source install mode for `puggers`.
    item(status="open") Determine whether to use NAPI-RS tooling directly, a small custom install script, or a node-gyp wrapper around Cargo.
    item(status="open") Decide what reproducibility proof or comparison workflow should accompany locally built artifacts.
